The huge win is with the Orc Rogue.

No alignment problem and the stat limits are not crippling for the
role.

In exchange you get infravision, starting food, pizza resistance (no
starting cloak for rogues to protect you against spicy meatballs
tossed by Italian gnomes) and a breakup of Orc hordes into half non-
hostiles so that you can save some for later when you encounter a
neutered or lame altar or just need chow.

The big defect of the Orc Rogue is that elves are hostile and they
tend to be difficult at early levels.

